    {
      "reference": "H1744",
      "topic_key": "when.capture.begins",
      "source_document": "WORK_NOTES/A19_PRIOR_ANSWERS_REVIEW_20260914/PRESERVED_ANSWERS.md",
      "source_evidence_document": "WORK_NOTES/A19_PRIOR_ANSWERS_REVIEW_20260914/PRESERVED_ANSWER_EVIDENCE.json",
      "source_record": "nh_interview_state.disconnected-before-full-restart",
      "event_seq": 1744,
      "event_sha256": "4375f2f44892730938baa017f20014c753d5fe663647cec8c2e99511591cd7c5",
      "original_answer_timestamp": null,
      "review_date": "2026-09-14",
      "answer_sha256": "9ea0ec04db3feb3e636245360c1ccee2375b9873ebb410d1540464606f36d600",
      "answer_utf8_bytes": 229,
      "explicitly_replaces_prior_answer": false,
      "replaces_reference": null,
      "answer_text": "For each device, I can allow camera or VR use, block it, or change that later. N.H may begin automatically only on a device I have already approved. A new or blocked device must not use it just because another device is approved."
    },
    {
      "reference": "H1745",
      "topic_key": "what.is.captured",
      "source_document": "WORK_NOTES/A19_PRIOR_ANSWERS_REVIEW_20260914/PRESERVED_ANSWERS.md",
      "source_evidence_document": "WORK_NOTES/A19_PRIOR_ANSWERS_REVIEW_20260914/PRESERVED_ANSWER_EVIDENCE.json",
      "source_record": "nh_interview_state.disconnected-before-full-restart",
      "event_seq": 1745,
      "event_sha256": "825dcf137197c379777d7c4328ae07996a59522dec76d092a2959d2fde7447a7",
      "original_answer_timestamp": null,
      "review_date": "2026-09-14",
      "answer_sha256": "030864c2b0254735122b156b84c968ad8f517f15aab807e9edc0466e42035e32",
      "answer_utf8_bytes": 230,
      "explicitly_replaces_prior_answer": false,
      "replaces_reference": null,
      "answer_text": "On an approved device, N.H may remember useful observations and sometimes save meaningful photos or videos automatically. I can tell it what to save, what not to save, or remove it later. A new or blocked device has no permission."
    },
    {
      "reference": "H1747",
      "topic_key": "what.remains.transient",
      "source_document": "WORK_NOTES/A19_PRIOR_ANSWERS_REVIEW_20260914/PRESERVED_ANSWERS.md",
      "source_evidence_document": "WORK_NOTES/A19_PRIOR_ANSWERS_REVIEW_20260914/PRESERVED_ANSWER_EVIDENCE.json",
      "source_record": "nh_interview_state.disconnected-before-full-restart",
      "event_seq": 1747,
      "event_sha256": "95fbe35f382397eb1e2193f67f74bd88c0b923d2e284285ac5c66e7e967b972f",
      "original_answer_timestamp": null,
      "review_date": "2026-09-14",
      "answer_sha256": "26a2038e0caf1c266a473b0a48aa2a5ef9072749900031bfdc9ff34c95972fd2",
      "answer_utf8_bytes": 268,
      "explicitly_replaces_prior_answer": false,
      "replaces_reference": null,
      "answer_text": "N.H should decide what is useful to remember from approved capture and may keep meaningful observations, photos, or videos. I can tell it not to keep something, correct its choice, or remove it later. Unimportant raw capture can remain temporary instead of being kept."
    },
    {
      "reference": "H1749",
      "topic_key": "voice.and.gesture.combine",
      "source_document": "WORK_NOTES/A19_PRIOR_ANSWERS_REVIEW_20260914/PRESERVED_ANSWERS.md",
      "source_evidence_document": "WORK_NOTES/A19_PRIOR_ANSWERS_REVIEW_20260914/PRESERVED_ANSWER_EVIDENCE.json",
      "source_record": "nh_interview_state.disconnected-before-full-restart",
      "event_seq": 1749,
      "event_sha256": "14639c967759e0d442fc455484d7b8ae5061ad468886fb1ba8f257c0fdbc3f1f",
      "original_answer_timestamp": null,
      "review_date": "2026-09-14",
      "answer_sha256": "51b632b2316ce2fdec1786d63d76ab2e8cdd05c9fa49847b295d7b3d27122ee6",
      "answer_utf8_bytes": 236,
      "explicitly_replaces_prior_answer": false,
      "replaces_reference": null,
      "answer_text": "N.H should use the full context to combine voice and gestures. When the meaning is clear, it acts without interrupting me. When it is genuinely unsure or the signals conflict, it asks me instead of guessing, and I can always correct it."
    },
    {
      "reference": "H1750",
      "topic_key": "tracking.failure.behavior",
      "source_document": "WORK_NOTES/A19_PRIOR_ANSWERS_REVIEW_20260914/PRESERVED_ANSWERS.md",
      "source_evidence_document": "WORK_NOTES/A19_PRIOR_ANSWERS_REVIEW_20260914/PRESERVED_ANSWER_EVIDENCE.json",
      "source_record": "nh_interview_state.disconnected-before-full-restart",
      "event_seq": 1750,
      "event_sha256": "6dab612b4cccfb28dae54b693d9fa511aaf87f7789b2ed7e20546a45e73e63f4",
      "original_answer_timestamp": null,
      "review_date": "2026-09-14",
      "answer_sha256": "d4c85f5dc8036bc9b2c79acb9e83f24c2fb4085ae63acd501c2d7eb9523b9ee3",
      "answer_utf8_bytes": 214,
      "explicitly_replaces_prior_answer": false,
      "replaces_reference": null,
      "answer_text": "If a gesture is unclear or tracking fails, N.H should choose what to do based on how serious the problem is and tell me what is happening. It must ask me instead of guessing when the meaning is genuinely uncertain."
    },
    {
      "reference": "H1752",
      "topic_key": "evidence.reconstruction.invention.labeling",
      "source_document": "WORK_NOTES/A19_PRIOR_ANSWERS_REVIEW_20260914/PRESERVED_ANSWERS.md",
      "source_evidence_document": "WORK_NOTES/A19_PRIOR_ANSWERS_REVIEW_20260914/PRESERVED_ANSWER_EVIDENCE.json",
      "source_record": "nh_interview_state.disconnected-before-full-restart",
      "event_seq": 1752,
      "event_sha256": "8c51c2f17ad90e8622bb87a67fa564d3d3742f317f502053e190952b8de05b9f",
      "original_answer_timestamp": null,
      "review_date": "2026-09-14",
      "answer_sha256": "c02f7ebc6a22e38899bee1f9c7bca54decc2fbfc405a89d50fe6c74cc46b6c66",
      "answer_utf8_bytes": 29,
      "explicitly_replaces_prior_answer": false,
      "replaces_reference": null,
      "answer_text": "Leave it blank... And, ask me"
    },
    {
      "reference": "H1753",
      "topic_key": "evidence.reconstruction.invention.labeling",
      "source_document": "WORK_NOTES/A19_PRIOR_ANSWERS_REVIEW_20260914/PRESERVED_ANSWERS.md",
      "source_evidence_document": "WORK_NOTES/A19_PRIOR_ANSWERS_REVIEW_20260914/PRESERVED_ANSWER_EVIDENCE.json",
      "source_record": "nh_interview_state.disconnected-before-full-restart",
      "event_seq": 1753,
      "event_sha256": "a46c3037bcffebbea3170bcfe59eb5f738c26fba6bb25cd6df57fb684f9e3c88",
      "original_answer_timestamp": null,
      "review_date": "2026-09-14",
      "answer_sha256": "06527a5170832c0b5093729577b1c8e8e65ee5e65f749643bd43f372a017a946",
      "answer_utf8_bytes": 223,
      "explicitly_replaces_prior_answer": true,
      "replaces_reference": "H1752",
      "answer_text": "N.H should rebuild childhood memories from the real memories, photos, videos, notes, and other evidence I have available. If the available material does not show something, leave it blank and ask me instead of inventing it."
    },
    {
      "reference": "H1754",
      "topic_key": "memory.replay.vs.simulation.visual.difference",
      "source_document": "WORK_NOTES/A19_PRIOR_ANSWERS_REVIEW_20260914/PRESERVED_ANSWERS.md",
      "source_evidence_document": "WORK_NOTES/A19_PRIOR_ANSWERS_REVIEW_20260914/PRESERVED_ANSWER_EVIDENCE.json",
      "source_record": "nh_interview_state.disconnected-before-full-restart",
      "event_seq": 1754,
      "event_sha256": "feaf51c6ea8c669bbb780ef62a33971c141189dbcefd004a284624d49ee085f1",
      "original_answer_timestamp": null,
      "review_date": "2026-09-14",
      "answer_sha256": "f017d4882671b195c88db1d5c130751bfc38900a45984bc8fbd1285a1ec6f097",
      "answer_utf8_bytes": 361,
      "explicitly_replaces_prior_answer": false,
      "replaces_reference": null,
      "answer_text": "While I am talking with N.H inside the experience, N.H should remind me whether it is a real memory replay or a simulation. In a simulation, N.H should speak about what I want to do in this simulation and how I want to do it, so the simulation context stays clear. It should also show a clear visible sign, but I will decide the exact design of that sign later."
    },
    {
      "reference": "H1756",
      "topic_key": "visibility.of.the.rest.of.the.world",
      "source_document": "WORK_NOTES/A19_PRIOR_ANSWERS_REVIEW_20260914/PRESERVED_ANSWERS.md",
      "source_evidence_document": "WORK_NOTES/A19_PRIOR_ANSWERS_REVIEW_20260914/PRESERVED_ANSWER_EVIDENCE.json",
      "source_record": "nh_interview_state.disconnected-before-full-restart",
      "event_seq": 1756,
      "event_sha256": "9cb5229b8a16954691da4a4ca0d3a0449cea0fe2d62584d7de0826f56660a88d",
      "original_answer_timestamp": null,
      "review_date": "2026-09-14",
      "answer_sha256": "c73d58cdda351596f1ef0cec1440c5317181a1ba3cf90fa3a83c98f2aed900c5",
      "answer_utf8_bytes": 130,
      "explicitly_replaces_prior_answer": false,
      "replaces_reference": null,
      "answer_text": "N.H should adapt how visible the rest of Ness’s World is based on the situation, and I can always change or override its choice."
    },
    {
      "reference": "H1757",
      "topic_key": "full.learning.history",
      "source_document": "WORK_NOTES/A19_PRIOR_ANSWERS_REVIEW_20260914/PRESERVED_ANSWERS.md",
      "source_evidence_document": "WORK_NOTES/A19_PRIOR_ANSWERS_REVIEW_20260914/PRESERVED_ANSWER_EVIDENCE.json",
      "source_record": "nh_interview_state.disconnected-before-full-restart",
      "event_seq": 1757,
      "event_sha256": "646ef686855ba9233d9d3cf187bc2924be50b257e6e778c6acf3dd8315554e69",
      "original_answer_timestamp": null,
      "review_date": "2026-09-14",
      "answer_sha256": "3520f767ba2d34ae5df1ff0ea1da15a8e2f0a80ad00db47c36511ad61e382ed0",
      "answer_utf8_bytes": 317,
      "explicitly_replaces_prior_answer": false,
      "replaces_reference": null,
      "answer_text": "N.H should decide what part of my learning history to show first based on the feature I am using, the situation, what I am trying to do, and what my past corrections taught it. The full history must remain available, I can always ask for something different, and my correction should teach N.H what to show next time."
    },
    {
      "reference": "H1759",
      "topic_key": "branching.and.reset",
      "source_document": "WORK_NOTES/A19_PRIOR_ANSWERS_REVIEW_20260914/PRESERVED_ANSWERS.md",
      "source_evidence_document": "WORK_NOTES/A19_PRIOR_ANSWERS_REVIEW_20260914/PRESERVED_ANSWER_EVIDENCE.json",
      "source_record": "nh_interview_state.disconnected-before-full-restart",
      "event_seq": 1759,
      "event_sha256": "3ed7aaa9817deb2de32cf92cc4c1a473a968cf38c9d531965b13d6041d101091",
      "original_answer_timestamp": null,
      "review_date": "2026-09-14",
      "answer_sha256": "c45fc6e8253fc10f79d8722b83be2d52adb678983ca5e4ab885b7fea02df13c5",
      "answer_utf8_bytes": 220,
      "explicitly_replaces_prior_answer": false,
      "replaces_reference": null,
      "answer_text": "Inside simulations, N.H should permanently remember the complete path and everything that happened automatically, so I can always go back to any earlier point and try another path without having to ask N.H to save first."
    },
    {
      "reference": "H1760",
      "topic_key": "challenges.or.limits.one.learned.pattern",
      "source_document": "WORK_NOTES/A19_PRIOR_ANSWERS_REVIEW_20260914/PRESERVED_ANSWERS.md",
      "source_evidence_document": "WORK_NOTES/A19_PRIOR_ANSWERS_REVIEW_20260914/PRESERVED_ANSWER_EVIDENCE.json",
      "source_record": "nh_interview_state.disconnected-before-full-restart",
      "event_seq": 1760,
      "event_sha256": "32638f9399f6863c9e8cdf0f0e9f2634ce4a7eecdf4d3c6bc6c5a8acb495fe9b",
      "original_answer_timestamp": null,
      "review_date": "2026-09-14",
      "answer_sha256": "ec5944985c397c80fb31930583a44ddde7ba55d693660140b89e036a24da5ba4",
      "answer_utf8_bytes": 319,
      "explicitly_replaces_prior_answer": false,
      "replaces_reference": null,
      "answer_text": "When I correct or limit one thing N.H has learned about me, N.H should preserve my exact correction and its full context. It should apply the correction itself when my meaning is clear, ask me only when it is genuinely unsure, and my choice must always override N.H. My corrections should teach it what to do next time."
    },
    {
      "reference": "H1762",
      "topic_key": "time.controls",
      "source_document": "WORK_NOTES/A19_PRIOR_ANSWERS_REVIEW_20260914/PRESERVED_ANSWERS.md",
      "source_evidence_document": "WORK_NOTES/A19_PRIOR_ANSWERS_REVIEW_20260914/PRESERVED_ANSWER_EVIDENCE.json",
      "source_record": "nh_interview_state.disconnected-before-full-restart",
      "event_seq": 1762,
      "event_sha256": "9e63975009b7c53d9921f30ca6ca8c4609855fbe8354e7e89233580d304fad12",
      "original_answer_timestamp": null,
      "review_date": "2026-09-14",
      "answer_sha256": "31694478d76f3d21117f0ac427ee18da0561fb715d12997d6c47eb1047aeb755",
      "answer_utf8_bytes": 237,
      "explicitly_replaces_prior_answer": false,
      "replaces_reference": null,
      "answer_text": "At any time, Ness can independently open, close, or lock N.H.'s authority over each simulation control. N.H. may act only within the permission currently granted, and Ness can change that permission before, during, or after a simulation."
    },
    {
