      "explicitly_replaces_prior_answer": true,
      "replaces_reference": "H1762",
      "answer_text": "As a non-negotiable global rule for simulations, N.H has standing default permission to act within and manipulate the simulation space across every current and future simulation-related feature. When Ness gives a specific or general request, N.H may carry it out using relevant material from Ness’s memory, other available sources, and the internet, while preserving all existing evidence, privacy, provenance, and authority boundaries. Ness can explicitly refuse any action or close or lock this permission at any time. A refusal blocks the action concerned; the standing permission otherwise remains in effect unless Ness closes or locks it for longer. Ness’s explicit choice always overrides N.H."
